{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices","id":1089386,"title":"C20 Tone deaf art choices?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-07T14:32:12-07:00","id":1089386,"title":"C20 Tone deaf art choices?","content":"For the most part, I'm happy and excited about C20, after my first read through of the PDF. There were two art choices that smack me as, at the very least, a bit tone deaf.<br /> Those would be the pieces for the eshu (p. 92) and redcap (p. 100). <br /> <br /> If I am being generous, I can possibly see the eshu as attempting to be more middle-eastern, but that strains credulity. A kith that is described as taking their name from a Yoruba trickster spirit has basically been whitewashed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, one of the most celtic in origin of all the fae, the redcap, is suddenly now a black thug. The implications here are mind-boggling, and I don't like the fact that the most violent and thuggish of the kiths is the one of the only representations of poc in the kith pages. (I'm not sure what the boggan is; it is the only other one that could be.)<br /> <br /> All in all, a great book. I just think that somebody fell asleep on those two pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13407-dybbuk67","name":"dybbuk67","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T18:12:11-07:00","id":1089502,"title":"","content":"I always thought Dice was biracial? c oulda sworn thats his writeup in Toj? i cant say anything about the boggan and redcap though....<br /> <br /> ah KB Eshu does actually say that his current face is that of a white man, so the art is correct the choice for him as a Sig is the issue then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","user":"CameraObscura83","date":".  Fact checking 05-07-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T22:30:17-07:00","id":1089585,"title":"","content":"I couldn't identify a signature character out of a lineup. Nor is it explained that these are signature characters. The game might actually be picked up by people who have never seen Changeling before. Certainly there will be reviewers who aren't aware of the in-joke. The images need to stand on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13407-dybbuk67","name":"dybbuk67","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-07T23:15:43-07:00","id":1089601,"title":"","content":"i only know it's Dice because they name him above the list in the sterotypes secton on the eshu page.I do agree odd choice to choose him as the Eshu sig though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T01:37:28-07:00","id":1089640,"title":"","content":"Well I see it as technically possible as the Kithain seem to spread to other Cultures, and after the 13 Kithain acknowledged each other and joined together they started to share each others cultures, and after breeding with different new cultures they start to infect those cultures. At the basic level all it takes is breed with humans of those cultures, and possibly after that happens they might even be born outside of those bloodlines with reincarnation osmosis.<br /> <br /> Certain Kiths, such as Satyrs and Pooka seem to have had an easier and earlier time spreading into other cultures of people, but I think by being one of the 13 Kithain all the Kiths, even the very culturally attached Clurichaun are starting to spread.<br /> <br /> Like I would imagine at the Start Trolls were tied exclusively to the Norse/Germanic Cultures that inspired their legends but then spread throughout europe to all giant dreams, and by the time of the Present they exist worldwide, with an apparent line coming from Iberia to Duke Topaz in Mexico. Same with the Confusing House Issue. We have a Middle Eastern Padshah with a Welsh House they are nobility of.<br /> <br /> This is why I would like other Noble Houses, perhaps non Sidhe Noble Houses started by Gallain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T03:31:46-07:00","id":1089680,"title":"","content":"I have more gripes with how mundane they all look. Piskies, Selkies kinda fine.<br /> <br /> Clurichauns, Sidhe (both), and pretty much everyone look, like LARPers with elven ears.<br /> <br /> Compare that to Thallain arts.<br /> <br /> Compare boggan with gorgeous Di Terlizzi works.<br /> <br /> And kith that has inhuman traits... Satyr has something weird with their spine. Troll signature looks nothing, like trolls in their Kithbook, male or female. Redcaps had a specific style, recurrent across the books, now they have Cthulhu growing on their face. I'm not sure about Pooka art. I mean, I'm all about breaking stereotypes and you may say, that Pooka suffer from Fishmalk reputation, but it could've been so cool joke if text reflected that - when I was scrolling the page I was expecting to see something like Schrodinger from Hellsing OVA, not Wolverine Knock-Off. And don't get me started on Sluagh and their signature style is thrown out of the window...<br /> <br /> What's important is that for changelings, kith is their race. And many Redcaps (Eiluned, Liam, Sluah) are experiencing distrust and discrimination. Being black Redcap only adds to the pool. Now, I would've left Redcap black, but put him in the rich lawyer suit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> and added Cheshire Cat grin on his face.<br /> <br /> Even in the land of dreams, others think of you as a ganger and monster... Isn't that shitty? Isn't that unfair? Rising above what's expected of you, would be ten times as hard. But you have a dream and determination. You'll use every opportunity, every advantage at your disposal. You'll use your mundane influence to teach Sidhe, that you're not to be trifled with. You'll use your changeling gifts to outperform your mortal competition. They don't believe in magic? Lack of belief doesn't pardon them from consequences. Some might say, that what you do is questionable. You say: unconventional. And smile, always smile. Let them be always... on edge.<br /> <br /> Tell, how would <i><b>you</b></i> draw the signature characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-08-2017, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T08:34:54-07:00","id":1089804,"title":"","content":"That Voldemort Sluagh... ugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T09:35:16-07:00","id":1089831,"title":"","content":"The eshu character is supposed to be Dice, and he's described in my art notes as Middle Eastern. I have no idea why he's so white, though I do know that the art-folks had trouble finding pictures of Dice. <br /> <br /> As far as the rest of the characters, I'm kind of embarrassed about how white they all turned out to be. I specified race for a few of them (redcap, boggan, selkie, Autumn sidhe, a couple of the others), but every characters I <i>didn't</i> specify a race was depicted as white. Now, I've been doing this long enough to know that's what would happen, so I absolutely should have specified that a few more of the kith pictures be POC. Mea culpa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T10:23:42-07:00","id":1089849,"title":"","content":"So the black thug redcap was a specific choice? Also, I believe you on the autumn sidhe and the selkie, but those are the most white latinos I've ever seen, if that is what the choice was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13407-dybbuk67","name":"dybbuk67","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T11:12:50-07:00","id":1089863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089831#post1089831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The eshu character is supposed to be Dice, and he's described in my art notes as Middle Eastern. I have no idea why he's so white, though I do know that the art-folks had trouble finding pictures of Dice.<br /> <br /> As far as the rest of the characters, I'm kind of embarrassed about how white they all turned out to be. I specified race for a few of them (redcap, boggan, selkie, Autumn sidhe, a couple of the others), but every characters I <i>didn't</i> specify a race was depicted as white. Now, I've been doing this long enough to know that's what would happen, so I absolutely should have specified that a few more of the kith pictures be POC. Mea culpa.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dice in KB eshu is described as white for what its worth, or that he wears a white face (which seemed odd as he was soichain too?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:21:19-07:00","id":1089884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089863#post1089863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dice in KB eshu is described as white for what its worth, or that he wears a white face (which seemed odd as he was soichain too?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Dice actually makes sense in light of that.<br /> <br /> Was the boggan black or South Asian? I figured he could be either. The selkie looks possibly Latina, possibly Inuit or Sami (which would make sense, given that they're seal fae).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T12:57:20-07:00","id":1089910,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the sluagh pic. She doesn't look like you can break her in half. The selkie's mortal race I wasn't sure of, though it's a nice pic. The Black redcap was fine with me -- she has grey-tinged skin, if you look closely -- though her mouth looks really odd. I was just happy to see a female redcap and one who's a woman of color, though the implications seem somewhat unfortunate. Can you tweak the skin color of some of the kith before the final pdf, Matt? Of would that not be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T13:25:44-07:00","id":1089920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dybbuk67</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089849#post1089849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the black thug redcap was a specific choice? Also, I believe you on the autumn sidhe and the selkie, but those are the most white latinos I've ever seen, if that is what the choice was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I guess I don't read her as &quot;thug,&quot; just as a redcap. <br /> <br /> Autumn sidhe and selkie were specified as white (well, selkie as &quot;pale skin,&quot; anyway) because they're specific characters. There were a couple of others that I didn't specify that wound up white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:05:55-07:00","id":1089946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089910#post1089910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually liked the sluagh pic. She doesn't look like you can break her in half.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should say that, I thought the same about the Selkie. She's a seal in human form, of course she's not thin.<br /> <br /> Though by seal terms she's positively emaciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T14:47:02-07:00","id":1089976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089910#post1089910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually liked the sluagh pic. She doesn't look like you can break her in half. The selkie's mortal race I wasn't sure of, though it's a nice pic. The Black redcap was fine with me -- she has grey-tinged skin, if you look closely -- though her mouth looks really odd. I was just happy to see a female redcap and one who's a woman of color, though the implications seem somewhat unfortunate. Can you tweak the skin color of some of the kith before the final pdf, Matt? Of would that not be possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, you can't break Sluagh in half, they are flexible, as snakes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 05-11-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T15:02:18-07:00","id":1089985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089946#post1089946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Funny you should say that, I thought the same about the Selkie. She's a seal in human form, of course she's not thin.<br /> <br /> Though by seal terms she's positively emaciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're lacking the real plus-sized kithain. I think the artist has some very fit models. There are lots of hunky young blokes with slightly pointy ears, all of a similar age. The least human-looking kith portraits look the best, I think. But the artwork everywhere else is spectacular and much more diverse. In general, I hated the V20 splat art (V20DA was great though), so this is an improvement. You can't please everyone, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:46:09-07:00","id":1090055,"title":"","content":"I also liked the selkie pic too, for much the same reasons. In the past, most sluagh pics looked like noodle people, or else literally two dimensional. Which makes them look far too breakable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T21:20:42-07:00","id":1090108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090055#post1090055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also liked the selkie pic too, for much the same reasons. In the past, most sluagh pics looked like noodle people, or else literally two dimensional. Which makes them look far too breakable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noodle people, you say? Time to get CLAMP on things... (^VVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:28:11-07:00","id":1090145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089985#post1089985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're lacking the real plus-sized kithain. I think the artist has some very fit models. There are lots of hunky young blokes with slightly pointy ears, all of a similar age. The least human-looking kith portraits look the best, I think. But the artwork everywhere else is spectacular and much more diverse. In general, I hated the V20 splat art (V20DA was great though), so this is an improvement. You can't please everyone, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see the book so far, but thought about it, when saw the sneak peaks and from what I read here it could be exactly the same case for me as V20. Most of the artworks are good, or at least okay, but most of the splats... ugh. They are just too mundane and even the ones which aren't are not really my cup of tea stylistically. I didn't really like V20DA for the same reason, but it was a bit better, I agree. W20 and M20 were much-much better. I think it could be much more glaring in the case of C20, because the kithain are really ought to be fantastical, IMO.<br /> <br /> The &quot;LARPers with pointy ears&quot; remark got me wondering if WW had a hand in that, but ultimately, don't think so and Tuesday isn't conspiracy theory day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:54:13-07:00","id":1090161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1089920#post1089920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I guess I don't read her as &quot;thug,&quot; just as a redcap.<br /> <br /> Autumn sidhe and selkie were specified as white (well, selkie as &quot;pale skin,&quot; anyway) because they're specific characters. There were a couple of others that I didn't specify that wound up white.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah she just seemed redcap to me, no problem with it. The Eshu actually seems asiany to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T02:56:40-07:00","id":1090197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090161#post1090161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah she just seemed redcap to me, no problem with it. The Eshu actually seems asiany to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Asians are the most underrepresented in the book. Seems like there's a decent number of black characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T09:59:54-07:00","id":1090760,"title":"","content":"The eshu reads Asian to me, as well, so I'm glad some other folks are seeing that. Also on the bandwagon that the redcap doesn't read as thug to me, just as redcap. I also really love the sluagh, she reads the most <i>faerie</i> to me. I think if I were to change anything it would be make one of the sidhe a person of color (the Arcadian one, I suppose, since the Autumn one is specifically white). Depicting the most beautiful creature in the Dreaming as a person of color is a great message. All in all, though, I thought the kith pictures were well done (love the troll soccer mom), though I'd agree that some of them aren't really evocative of <i>faerie. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:04:24-07:00","id":1090764,"title":"","content":"I thought the arcadian sidhe was hispanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T10:14:44-07:00","id":1090769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090764#post1090764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the arcadian sidhe was hispanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With you bringing that up I actually really see her as latina. Thank you! It's cool how art draws different interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-10T13:53:37-07:00","id":1090854,"title":"","content":"Glad I'm not the only one who was reading the Eshu as Asian. <br /> <br /> I don't think people were saying that the artwork made the Redcap look thuggish, just that maybe it wasn't the best idea to associate the Kith that's stereotyped as angry, violent criminals with a real world group that faces the same prejudices, especially since it's one of the only Kiths to be associated with that group of people by the artwork.<br /> <br /> Does anybody know if OPP specifically tells its artists that they're looking to showcase diversity in their art? I know in a perfect world they shouldn't have to specify, but I've heard tons of stories (not about OPP that I'm aware of, mind you) on social media and in online art communities where artists have submitted artwork featuring non-white or plus-size figures when ethnicity and/or body type weren't specified only to have clients request alterations to make the character white and/or thin (usually in coded language). Since many artists have experienced this and it's a pretty well-known phenomenon in the industry, a lot of artists will go with white, thin, traditionally beautiful characters because they've learned that that's what clients normally want when they don't specify anything else, not because it's the artist's personal preference, and they can't afford to devote the time and energy to trying something that will likely be rejected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T03:02:35-07:00","id":1091036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090854#post1090854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad I'm not the only one who was reading the Eshu as Asian. <br /> <br /> I don't think people were saying that the artwork made the Redcap look thuggish, just that maybe it wasn't the best idea to associate the Kith that's stereotyped as angry, violent criminals with a real world group that faces the same prejudices, especially since it's one of the only Kiths to be associated with that group of people by the artwork.<br /> <br /> Does anybody know if OPP specifically tells its artists that they're looking to showcase diversity in their art? I know in a perfect world they shouldn't have to specify, but I've heard tons of stories (not about OPP that I'm aware of, mind you) on social media and in online art communities where artists have submitted artwork featuring non-white or plus-size figures when ethnicity and/or body type weren't specified only to have clients request alterations to make the character white and/or thin (usually in coded language). Since many artists have experienced this and it's a pretty well-known phenomenon in the industry, a lot of artists will go with white, thin, traditionally beautiful characters because they've learned that that's what clients normally want when they don't specify anything else, not because it's the artist's personal preference, and they can't afford to devote the time and energy to trying something that will likely be rejected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear that. The eshu has vaguely Russian looks for me, I guess, but it's the hair colour that mostly makes me read him as white. I also read the Arcadian sidhe as Latina. But race is as much what you look for as what's there.<br /> <br /> I'm relatively light-skinned, so when I'm in Florida people think I'm Hispanic. When I'm in Europe, people think I'm Italian. In the Spanish Caribbean I'm Latino. I've been seen as Jewish, South Asian and even just white.<br /> <br /> My maternal granddad is from St. Kitts (he's Afro-Caribbean, but claimed Spanish, Portuguese, Scottish and Jewish descent depending on which story he was telling...), and my maternal grandmother was English of Irish descent. My paternal grandparents, I think, are English with some Middle Eastern ancestry. Because I grew up in a West Indian/Caribbean community, however, with a mother who looks black, people who know me have always called me black.<br /> <br /> In other words, I guess we all impose what we expect to see on what we do see, to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:15:41-07:00","id":1091054,"title":"","content":"Not having the pdf nor pictures of what is being discussed, I get the feeling that what everyone is saying is that the art (with a few exceptions) still sucks. I look at the Claurican and it looks like an ordinary person. So sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4045-princeofcincinnati","name":"princeofcincinnati","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4045_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:25:35-07:00","id":1091057,"title":"","content":"I like the art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:47:13-07:00","id":1091062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>princeofcincinnati</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091054#post1091054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not having the pdf nor pictures of what is being discussed, I get the feeling that what everyone is saying is that the art (with a few exceptions) still sucks. I look at the Claurican and it looks like an ordinary person. So sad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the art is spectacular. The splat art is a little . . . Banal. Very few of them actually look like faeries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T04:54:15-07:00","id":1091065,"title":"","content":"I think those are very good pictures of their mortal seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:31:31-07:00","id":1091094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090161#post1090161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah she just seemed redcap to me, no problem with it. The Eshu actually seems asiany to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, this doesn't change the fact that the picture goes along with a very harmful (as in gets black people murdrered) stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:45:29-07:00","id":1091100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091065#post1091065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those are very good pictures of their mortal seemings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but without the intent of being offensive: what's the point?<br /> <br /> That is one of my main problems with a lot of artworks in OPP's books, both WoD and CofD, that frequently the characters look like just ordinary people (for example, tanned vampires, or just too normal-looking vampires). I get the representation and connectivity angle, but in a book about supernatural creatures, I want to see supernatural creatures and that's doubly so in a game about fairies. I see normal people every day.<br /> <br /> Now, I don't have the book, so my impression is just what I got from the art sneak peeks in the official blog and there, but I got the same vibe, that most of the art is really great, but the splats are too mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:00:42-07:00","id":1091107,"title":"","content":"There is a more fantasy version of all the Kithain on pages 48-49. It's done by the same person who did the Thallain illustrations.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit to add:</b> AND! It has the greatest illustration in the whole book \u2014 Pinkie Pie the Party Piskie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 05-11-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:07:59-07:00","id":1091110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091107#post1091107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a more fantasy version of all the Kithain on pages 48-49. It's done by the same person who did the Thallain illustrations.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit to add:</b> AND! It has the greatest illustration in the whole book \u2014 Pinkie Pie the Party Piskie! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those should have been the splat pics. They're cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T07:19:37-07:00","id":1091114,"title":"","content":"It's a range of tones. Is your chronicle a low budget but incredibly fun urban fantasy TV show along the lines of Lost Girl? Or is your chronicle a spared no expense CG heavy blockbuster like Oz the Great and Powerful? Both are awesome, but which you prefer is up to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T11:53:31-07:00","id":1091215,"title":"","content":"The Redcap and Sluagh on p. 49 actually look more like normal people/less fantastical than the art in the kith section. Personally, I like certain kiths better in the art on 48-49 and certain kiths better in the art in the kith sections, but I tend to like the urban fantasy asthetic. I kind of wish that either depiction of Redcaps had the &quot;gray, rubbery skin&quot; from the description.<br /> <br /> I hadn't noticed Pinkie Pie the Party Piskie before. That's pretty funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T13:03:04-07:00","id":1091239,"title":"","content":"My issue with the redcap picture in the kith section is except for her mouth she, doesn't have any redcap physical features. It's neither her mortal nor fae seeming, but rather something in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:11:04-07:00","id":1091267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091239#post1091239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My issue with the redcap picture in the kith section is except for her mouth she, doesn't have any redcap physical features. It's neither her mortal nor fae seeming, but rather something in between.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think they're all supposed to be the fae seeming, except maybe the Clurichaun. Unless they all have slipped seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:38:17-07:00","id":1091272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091094#post1091094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately, this doesn't change the fact that the picture goes along with a very harmful (as in gets black people murdrered) stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? <br /> <br /> Explain to me how an illustration of a black woman with obviously exaggerated fantasy-monster teeth taking a bite of a beer mug is going to get anyone murdered, please? <br /> <br /> I mean, I'll take the hit that there are too many white changelings in the splat art; I should have specified races for more of them, yes, that's on me. I'll even concede that more of them could have looked more obviously fae. But c'mon, now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:49:53-07:00","id":1091279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091272#post1091272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? <br /> <br /> Explain to me how an illustration of a black woman with obviously exaggerated fantasy-monster teeth taking a bite of a beer mug is going to get anyone murdered, please? <br /> <br /> I mean, I'll take the hit that there are too many white changelings in the splat art; I should have specified races for more of them, yes, that's on me. I'll even concede that more of them could have looked more obviously fae. But c'mon, now.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the sense that black men get killed by cops precisely because there's an excess of images of black people as thugs. It's a thing. I believe you 100% that it's not intentional, but the most depressing thing about stereotypes is that they usually aren't intentional but they appear anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:55:18-07:00","id":1091281,"title":"","content":"Some reading material:<br /> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Criminal_stereotype_of_African_Americans\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crim...ican_Americans</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2016/jul/12/black-men-america-violence-vulnerable-detroit\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theguardian.com/world/20...erable-detroit</a><br /> <a href=\"https://mappingpoliceviolence.org/unarmed/\" target=\"_blank\">https://mappingpoliceviolence.org/unarmed/</a><br /> <br /> It's not just that she's black. It's that the two black kiths are the domestic and the thug. When the Irish kith is also a drunken fighter, it's worrying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-11-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T14:58:58-07:00","id":1091285,"title":"","content":"Irish Privileges Engaged<br /> <br /> The Irish kith is the drunkard because that's what leprechauns are. If you expect to see stereotypes everywhere then you will and gods help us if you're charged with deciding when lethal force is applicable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T15:07:57-07:00","id":1091294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091281#post1091281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just that she's black. It's that the two black kiths are the domestic and the thug. When the Irish kith is also a drunken fighter, it's worrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that the author who handled the Clurichaun intentionally altered the rules/write-ups so that the Irish kith was not defined by the rules as drunkards. Their previous frailty was difficulty resisting alcohol and the effects of alcohol on their personality. The new frailty has nothing to do with drinking. I get what you're saying about the kiths visually represented in the book as POC being tied to racial stereotypes, but I'm really curious about your take on the Clurichaun. I just re-read the write-up in C20 and I'm not seeing anything which states that Clurichaun are drunkards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T16:59:26-07:00","id":1091336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091279#post1091279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the sense that black men get killed by cops precisely because there's an excess of images of black people as thugs. It's a thing. I believe you 100% that it's not intentional, but the most depressing thing about stereotypes is that they usually aren't intentional but they appear anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Art doesn't exist in a vacuum. The stereotypes of black people as violent, criminal, ugly, or subservient are real, widespread and harmful. Going along with those stereotypes reinforces them, even if it was not meant to do so.<br /> So while one picture is probably not going to get anyone murdered, it can contribute to keep alive the way of thinking that will.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T17:20:14-07:00","id":1091344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091336#post1091336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Art doesn't exist in a vacuum. The stereotypes of black people as violent, criminal, ugly, or subservient are real, widespread and harmful. Going along with those stereotypes reinforces them, even if it was not meant to do so.<br /> So while one picture is probably not going to get anyone murdered, it can contribute to keep alive the way of thinking that will.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, fair enough. I guess it might have helped to have more POC represented amongst the kith pictures, which, again, dammit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T20:48:56-07:00","id":1091408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091344#post1091344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, fair enough. I guess it might have helped to have more POC represented amongst the kith pictures, which, again, dammit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely recall hearing the former Exalted developers mention that you often need to twist the arms of artists and give them very specific instructions to avoid white-washing. Also, I guess in this case, stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T21:42:49-07:00","id":1091420,"title":"","content":"The splat art is really drab and lackluster compared to the splat art for Mage20 and Werewolf20. Like really bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3670-spook359","name":"Spook359","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3670_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:45:44-07:00","id":1091497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091408#post1091408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vaguely recall hearing the former Exalted developers mention that you often need to twist the arms of artists and give them very specific instructions to avoid white-washing. Also, I guess in this case, stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hiring a few non white artists would certainly help on that front. Deviant Art, Tumblr and even Twitter are full of very talented ones. Issues of diversity and representation are entirely man-made and easily solved by not denying minority groups an input.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:04:59-07:00","id":1091569,"title":"","content":"Aside from the questionable choice of making the Redcap black, which apparently wasn't the artist's decision, I personally really like most of this kith art. Yes, the figures depicted could be more diverse. I'm pretty sure this is the same artist and art director responsible for the amazing V20 clan artwork, which had better representation in my opinion, so I'm honestly curious what went differently here. <br /> <br /> (Also, am I the only one who thinks that the satyr looks vaguely Asian, too?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:42:19-07:00","id":1091687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091569#post1091569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the questionable choice of making the Redcap black, which apparently wasn't the artist's decision, I personally really like most of this kith art. Yes, the figures depicted could be more diverse. I'm pretty sure this is the same artist and art director responsible for the amazing V20 clan artwork, which had better representation in my opinion, so I'm honestly curious what went differently here.<br /> <br /> (Also, am I the only one who thinks that the satyr looks vaguely Asian, too?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't think there was anything vague about the satyr being Asian!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:18:05-07:00","id":1091700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091569#post1091569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the questionable choice of making the Redcap black, which apparently wasn't the artist's decision, I personally really like most of this kith art. Yes, the figures depicted could be more diverse. I'm pretty sure this is the same artist and art director responsible for the amazing V20 clan artwork, which had better representation in my opinion, so I'm honestly curious what went differently here.<br /> <br /> (Also, am I the only one who thinks that the satyr looks vaguely Asian, too?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not having seen the art notes for V20, I don't know, but my speculation would be that in V20, the art notes specified what characters' races should be. In C20, I put a note in the general art notes saying &quot;not all of these characters need to be white men, we can have POC and different gender presentations and body types&quot; (I'm paraphrasing), and I forgot that you really have to be specific in art notes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:08:58-07:00","id":1091721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091687#post1091687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I didn't think there was anything vague about the satyr being Asian!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the more I look at it, the more certain I am that that's totally an Asian Satyr.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:11:48-07:00","id":1091722,"title":"","content":"BTW, I totally miswrote Arcadian Sidhe when I meant to say Autumn Sidhe earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T16:14:33-07:00","id":1091748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1090197#post1090197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Asians are the most underrepresented in the book. Seems like there's a decent number of black characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Felt the same way. But then again, I'm Hispanic, and usually like my game worlds to be indicative of the real world in terms of race/ethnicity. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T23:31:16-07:00","id":1091841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091285#post1091285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irish Privileges Engaged<br /> <br /> The Irish kith is the drunkard because that's what leprechauns are. If you expect to see stereotypes everywhere then you will and gods help us if you're charged with deciding when lethal force is applicable.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Thankfully I wouldn't have to decide that. In my view, lethal force is never applicable. If you kill a criminal, they can't stand trial. If you kill an innocent person, you're a murderer. Everyone is innocent until proven guilty, so shooting anyone without a trial is murder.<br /> <br /> 2) You may have replied to my comment immediately, in which case you missed that I immediately updated that post to clarify that I meant drunken fighter to be clear (I wrote drunkard but it was more the violence that came through in the text). He's clearly a fighter. He's wearing an Irish flag on his T-shirt with blood flecks on him. His Birthright is starting fights. That is an Irish stereotype. Calling Irish privilege back at you, though, when I say this.<br /> <br /> Also, the book literally namedrops Black Lives Matters to make a point about the Shadow Court. But when we critically engage with the book using a core argument of groups like BLM, that's just looking for stereotypes? Nah. It's not an original idea of mine that stereotypes dehumanise, and that that makes it easier to kill minorities.<br /> <br /> To be fair, it's not just a C20 thing, and others have had this discussion elsewhere. All the 90s stuff had similar issues (the Brujah kith image was usually Theo Bell, a black bruiser; the whole concept of the Settites as black drug dealer serpent dudes; the Assamites; the Ravnos; etc). It's a legacy carried over in our nostalgia products. I'm not really blaming anyone, and it wasn't me who raised the initial point, but we also shouldn't pretend it's not there.<br /> <br /> As someone else pointed out in the thread, these are simple art issues that can be fixed by inviting POC to the decision-making process. I edit magazines all the time, and I manage one for a charity whose remit is diversity, so I literally have to go through and make sure that every race is featured, as well as the full spectrum of LGBT identities, disabled people, etc. I tell the designers this for my art notes, and they still don't always get it right the first time, so I send them back and they do it again until they get it right. In this case, we're using photography, and we have lots of photos to work with, but the basic framework is needed. I always pinpoint articles that might be contentious (domestic violence, mental health, cyberbullying), and then make notes to the designers to specifically avoid placing problematic images alongside them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, rant over. It's not enough to ruin the book for me--it's gorgeous. It's just a fair thing for us to point out, so that next time the next book can be even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 05-13-2017, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T05:52:07-07:00","id":1091918,"title":"","content":"What about the fact, that changelings are born of stereotypes? Good and bad.. Should we ignore that part, too? Get rid of all kiths as well? Listen.<br /> <br /> Their very race and strengths and weaknesses are typecasted by collective subconsciousness of humanity before they even born.<br /> <br /> I agree, that stereotypes dehumanize. That ideologies turn people's brains into mush, making them a living cogs, serving great machines of Great Ideas.<br /> <br /> Many people, and Changelings, I presume, embrace their stereotypes, are proud of them. Football clubs, universities, faculties, classes, nationalities, occupations, political parties, family clans, guilds, religions, cults, corporations, communities, and ideologies. Tribes. Some of are happy to live, work and die for their tribe and embrace the stereotypes. They embrace mocking-titles thrown at them and make them part of their identity.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer, that people not do that. That they would not stereotype others, not see the world in black and white and not turn themselves into a hivemind sockpuppets.<br /> <br /> But we live in a world, where they have a choice to do that.<br /> <br /> Troll stereotype of an honorable servant is no different from a leprechaun fighter or Sidhe ruler or Satyr party-goat. Or Boggan Hermit. Or Pooka Fool. Leprechauns of today are a stereotype of Irish people in 19th century. But nobody sees Leprechauns of modern media, as Irish people. They're Leprechauns. Faries. Spirits. Either malicious or benevolent, they are their own individual thing. Some embrace stereotypes, others - reject them furiously. Looking and acting like a particular stereotype no less representative, than not looking like it.<br /> <br /> Changeling: the Dreaming is a game about living embodiments of stereotypes. I think, its players can handle the idea of individuality and use this game as a tool to explore the riddles of human condition, and if they can't - their friends will help them. Have some trust in people.<br /> <br /> Sometimes <i>a cigar</i> is just a cigar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T10:30:24-07:00","id":1092000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firkraag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1089386-c20-tone-deaf-art-choices?p=1091918#post1091918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the fact, that changelings are born of stereotypes? Good and bad.. Should we ignore that part, too? Get rid of all kiths as well? Listen.<br /> <br /> Their very race and strengths and weaknesses are typecasted by collective subconsciousness of humanity before they even born.<br /> <br /> I agree, that stereotypes dehumanize. That ideologies turn people's brains into mush, making them a living cogs, serving great machines of Great Ideas.<br /> <br /> Many people, and Changelings, I presume, embrace their stereotypes, are proud of them. Football clubs, universities, faculties, classes, nationalities, occupations, political parties, family clans, guilds, religions, cults, corporations, communities, and ideologies. Tribes. Some of are happy to live, work and die for their tribe and embrace the stereotypes. They embrace mocking-titles thrown at them and make them part of their identity.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer, that people not do that. That they would not stereotype others, not see the world in black and white and not turn themselves into a hivemind sockpuppets.<br /> <br /> But we live in a world, where they have a choice to do that.<br /> <br /> Troll stereotype of an honorable servant is no different from a leprechaun fighter or Sidhe ruler or Satyr party-goat. Or Boggan Hermit. Or Pooka Fool. Leprechauns of today are a stereotype of Irish people in 19th century. But nobody sees Leprechauns of modern media, as Irish people. They're Leprechauns. Faries. Spirits. Either malicious or benevolent, they are their own individual thing. Some embrace stereotypes, others - reject them furiously. Looking and acting like a particular stereotype no less representative, than not looking like it.<br /> <br /> Changeling: the Dreaming is a game about living embodiments of stereotypes. I think, its players can handle the idea of individuality and use this game as a tool to explore the riddles of human condition, and if they can't - their friends will help them. Have some trust in people.<br /> <br /> Sometimes <i>a cigar</i> is just a cigar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Thanks, good points, IMO.<br /> <br /> It's really hard, the whole stereotypes thing, not just here, but in general. On the one hand bad stereotypes caused and are causing suffering and I totally understand, why people, especially members of the various minorities hate them and want to eradicate their uses. On the other hand, aside from what you wrote, which is true, I think, stereotypes are parts of our culture, so leaving them out entirely is not showing the world as it is. Also, I know plenty of people will hate me for saying it, but there it is: almost every stereotype became a stereotype for a reason and that's reason frequently (but not in every case) is that they have at least a shard of truth in them. Yes they're harmful in many cases, but they're also shedding light to the big trends of cultures or personality types, etc, from one point or the other.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying &quot;let's use negative stereotypes with wanton abandon&quot;, I don't want that. I'm happy that most of the problematic splats in WoD are more nuanced at this point. However, I think stereotypes are having their reason to exist and their uses.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}